@startuml
title Submission ordering and privacy
actor "Group A" as A
actor "Group B" as B
actor Teacher as T
participant "Socket.IO handlers" as S
participant "Synchronous reducer" as R
A -> S : join(empty group)
B -> S : join(same group)
S -> R : A join / validate session and phase
R -> R : bind A session to group atomically
R --> A : joined / group identity
S -> R : B join
R --> B : GROUP_OCCUPIED
B -> S : join(another empty group)
S -> R : validate B session and bind other group
R --> B : joined
note over A,R
Binding survives disconnect until activity ends.
Only original browser session can rejoin.
No teacher or student reassignment.
end note
A -> S : submit(requestId, questionId, all answers)
B -> S : submit(requestId, questionId, all answers)
S -> R : A command first at server boundary
alt wrong role, phase, item set or blank answer
 R --> A : safe rejection / no rank assigned
else valid complete payload
 R -> R : record time + increment sequence\nstore submission and first winner
 R --> A : own receipt only
 R --> T : teacher progress + tentative winners
end
S -> R : B command next
R -> R : same validations and ordered acceptance
R --> B : own receipt only
A -> S : retry same request
S -> R : check cached receipt
R --> A : original receipt / no new sequence
T -> S : end activity
S -> R : ordered end command
R -> R : phase Ended / freeze results
R --> A : published winners and all winning answers
R --> B : published winners and all winning answers
A -> S : late new submission
S -> R : validate current phase
R --> A : activity ended / no rank
note over S,R
No await between validation and mutation.
Socket timeout does not imply rejection.
Reconnect requests role-filtered snapshot.
Teacher reload gets currentActivityId from session.
end note
@enduml
